    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0089" n="75" xml:id="pg75"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indochina/1–1148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bonsal</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-11T22:00:00+01:00">January 11,
                            1948—10 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Foreign Minister<anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/> has just informed me that
                    Cabinet this afternoon authorized Dutch delegation <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Renville</hi> accept 6 points for political settlement offered by GOC
                    representing slight modification of points set forth January 9 to Helb by
                    Department officials (Deptel 9, January 9).<anchor n="2" xml:id="d52-f2"/>
                    Necessary authority telegraphed Batavia. Van Kleffens will inform
                        Department.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d52-f3"/> Foreign Minister states
                    Netherlands acceptance predicated on signature truce agreement and its
                    thorough-going implementation by Republic. Netherland Government has doubts re
                    feasibility provisions in 6 points relating plebiscites and representation in
                    USI accordance population. Cabinet unhappy at reference (reported by Helb) by
                    Department officials in conversation with Helb to ERP and to US assistance in
                    reconstruction Indonesia.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bonsal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d52-f1" n="1" xml:id="d52-f1-content">
                <p>Dr. C. G. W. H. Baron van Boetzelaer van Oosterhout.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f2" n="2" xml:id="d52-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram 10, January 9, 6 p. m., <ref target="#pg70">p. 70</ref>, and Batavia
                    telegram 22, January 6, 5 p. m., <ref target="#pg62">p. 62</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d52-f3" n="3" xml:id="d52-f3-content">
                <p>The Netherlands Embassy telephoned the information on January 12 to the
                    Department. (856e.00/l–1248)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
